  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef plans to go on a long drive, and is now checking whether he has enough fuel for the trip.\n\nChef's car has XXX units of fuel remaining.\n\nThe car has a fuel efficiency of YYY, meaning that for each unit of fuel it has, it can travel a distance of YYY kilometers.\n\nChef knows that the distance he needs to travel is exactly 100100100 kilometers.\n\nDoes he have enough fuel for his trip?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe only line of input will contain two space-separated integers XXX and YYY — the amount of fuel remaining and the car's fuel efficiency, respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer: `Yes` if Chef has enough fuel remaining, and `No` otherwise.\n\n\nEach character of the output can be printed in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e. the strings `NO`, `no`, `No`, and `nO` will all be treated as equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X,Y≤1001 \\le X, Y\\le 1001≤X,Y≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "10 13",
        "output": "Yes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are X=10X = 10X=10 units of fuel remaining.\nEach unit of fuel allows the car to travel for Y=13Y = 13Y=13 kilometers.\nSo, the total distance the car can travel equals 10×13=13010\\times 13 = 13010×13=130 kilometers.\nSince 130≥100130 \\ge 100130≥100, Chef has enough fuel for the trip."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5 8",
        "output": "No",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are X=5X = 5X=5 units of fuel remaining.\nEach unit of fuel allows the car to travel for Y=8Y = 8Y=8 kilometers.\nSo, the total distance the car can travel equals 5×8=405\\times 8 = 405×8=40 kilometers.\nSince 40<10040 \\lt 10040<100, Chef does not have enough fuel for the trip."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5 20",
        "output": "Yes",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ]
  },
